{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Your servants are twelve brothers.</b> At first they said, 'We are all sons of one man,' and they gave a reason why they were found gathered together: they said, because we are all sons of one man, therefore we gather together, none separating from his fellow. And furthermore, lest the grain be stolen by one of our attendants, therefore we all needed to come together." "<b>We are honest men.</b> Righteous men, sons of righteous men; we have never been spies. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: Joseph said to them, 'You entered through ten gates and now you are gathered in one place — this is nothing but the way of spies.' And now they said, 'Your servants are twelve brothers, sons of one man,' and they elaborated for him further, that they are ten, and the youngest is today with their father, and the one is no more, and they had gone to seek him. And Joseph answered, 'By this you shall be tested — by the life of Pharaoh, you shall not leave here unless your youngest brother comes,' and they found no answer to reply. And the answer of" "<b>By the life of Pharaoh.</b> One cannot say of Joseph the righteous that he swore falsely, nor do we find this at all; rather, he fulfilled his words in his oath every time. What he said, 'By the life of Pharaoh, that you are spies' — that is, since you say, 'the one is no more,' had you found him, what would you have done with him? They said to him: we would have redeemed him with any money assessed upon us. He said to them: and if they were not willing to give him for any money, what would you have done? They said to him: for this we came to kill or be killed. He said to them: 'By the life of Pharaoh, you are spies.' And likewise, 'By the life of Pharaoh, you shall not leave here' — he fulfilled his words, for Shimon remained behind and they did not all leave. And what they said, 'Your servants are twelve brothers,' it should have said 'we were,' for in the implication of אנחנו is that all are alive; but Scripture teaches that they prophesied unintentionally."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:19:49.180165844Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}